{"name":"Dark Humour","hex":"#661122","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark humour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of dark humor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark_humour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark humor","blocks":[{"text":"Dark humor, also known as black comedy, black humor, bleak comedy, dark comedy, gallows humor or morbid humor is a style of comedy that makes light of subject matter that is generally considered taboo as a topic for humor or laughter, particularly subjects that are normally considered serious or painful to discuss. Thus dark humor aims to provoke discomfort, serious thought, and uncomfortable amusement for its audience."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg/330px-Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_humor","wikidata":"Q53094"},{"title":"Humour","blocks":[{"text":"Humour or humor is the tendency of experiences to provoke laughter and provide amusement. The term derives from the humoral medicine of the ancient Greeks, which taught that the balance of fluids in the human body, known as \"humours\", controlled human health and emotion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Volunteer_Community_Relations_DVIDS190255.jpg/330px-Volunteer_Community_Relations_DVIDS190255.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humour","wikidata":"Q35874"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg/500px-Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg/500px-Hopscotch_to_oblivion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte